entry.summary:
If you want real-time visibility into network calls, WebSocket events, console logs, and analytics without leaving your app, @lokal-dev/react-native-bugbubble is a lightweight drop-in debugger for React Native. DEMO Floating debug bubble you can drag and tap to open the debugger UI. Tracks network, WebSocket, console, and analytics events out of the box. Zero native setup; pure JS/TS with sensible defaults. Configurable log limits, button position, and per-signal tracking. yarn add @lokal-dev/react-native-bugbubble # or npm install @lokal-dev/react-native-bugbubble
Add the component at your app root so it mounts once: import { BugBubbleProvider } from '@components/global/BugBubbleProvider';
export default function App() { return ( <> <YourApp /> <BugBubbleProvider /> …
